# KYC uploads — PII, must never be committed.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it must stay that way. Unanchored,
# `uploads/` matches a directory called `uploads` at ANY depth — so it also
# swallowed `src/common/uploads/`, and `stored-files.service.ts` was silently
# excluded from the commit that added it. Four files imported a module that was
# never pushed, and the repo did not compile for anyone who cloned it.
#
# git ignores quietly by design: `git add` reports nothing, `git status` shows
# nothing, and the gap only appears when the compiler looks for the file. A
# leading slash confines this to the upload directory at the repo root, which is
# the only one that ever holds PII.
/uploads/

# Claude Code: the shared harness (.claude/settings.json + hooks) IS committed,
# so the same gates run on every machine. Personal overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.vitest-result.json
